# Scraped corpus + HTTP cache (unlicensed source data, keep local)
data_pipeline/cache/
data_pipeline/out/

# NOTE: backend/idoma_dictionary_v3.json used to be ignored here, to avoid
# republishing idomaland.org pairs as a bulk download from a public repo. It is
# committed now, and since the corpus was merged in that decision does republish
# ~1,000 scraped English/Idoma pairs. Deliberate, and the tradeoff is:
#
#   * Keeping it ignored had a proven cost. Render builds from git, so every deploy
#     silently fell back to the fabricated v2 and served "òhụ" for house while the
#     model answered words the dictionary was supposed to cover. The Secret File that
#     was supposed to carry the dictionary instead was never added, and nothing in
#     /health said so.
#   * What ships is only the English/Idoma/dialect triples the lookup needs. The
#     scrape's `url` and `definition` fields -- the substance of idomaland.org's
#     pages -- stay unpublished under data_pipeline/out/ above, and idomaland.org is
#     credited in the README and on the model card.
#
# If that tradeoff is not acceptable for your fork, restore the ignore line and use a
# Render Secret File at /etc/secrets/idoma_dictionary_v3.json -- but then verify the
# deploy with `curl $URL/health` and check `dictionary_entries`, because that is the
# exact failure that went unnoticed before.

# TypeScript build artifacts
tsconfig.*.tsbuildinfo
